# Declared string exclusions for tool/version-control/hygiene.
#
# One `<path><TAB><literal string>` row per line, each preceded by a comment
# giving its reason. File-granularity exclusion is refused deliberately:
# docs/troubleshooting.md is the one file that has already drifted through
# this invariant, so blinding all of it would retire the check on its only
# real target.
#
# Enforced in both directions. A stale entry -- one whose literal no longer
# occurs at its path -- fails the check and names itself, so this file cannot
# become the place violations go to be forgotten.

# A Nix error message quoting a store path, where `programs` is a directory
# inside a flake rather than an account. The anchoring rule already excludes
# the line, because the character before the slash is a guillemet. The entry
# is declared so that widening the anchoring rule later cannot silently admit
# it unreviewed.
docs/troubleshooting.md	/home/programs/
